The public API must remain:

```rust
pub struct StampedDelta {
    pub position: u64,
    pub delta: i64,
}

pub fn combine_deltas(left: &[StampedDelta], right: &[StampedDelta]) -> Vec<StampedDelta>;
```

Both inputs are sorted by nondecreasing `position`. Combine them into one sorted sequence containing exactly one element per distinct position. Its `delta` must be the sum of every delta at that position across both inputs, including repeated positions within either input. Preserve entries whose summed delta is zero. All sums fit in `i64`.

The implementation must be deterministic, use only the Rust standard library, and perform no filesystem, network, clock, or random operations. Do not include a `main` function.

The current implementation incorrectly handles duplicate positions:

