```rust
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum MachinePhase {
    Offline,
    Intake,
    Processing,
    Release,
}

#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct MachineView {
    pub phase: MachinePhase,
    pub completed_batches: u64,
}

#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum MachineError {
    AlreadyRunning,
    Offline,
}

pub struct BatchMachine { /* private fields */ }

impl BatchMachine {
    pub fn new() -> Self;
    pub fn start(&mut self) -> Result<(), MachineError>;
    pub fn advance(&mut self) -> Result<(), MachineError>;
    pub fn stop(&mut self) -> Result<(), MachineError>;
    pub fn view(&self) -> MachineView;
}
```

A new machine is `Offline` with zero completed batches. `start` is valid only while offline and transitions to `Intake`; otherwise it returns `AlreadyRunning` without changing state. `advance` while active follows this cycle:

`Intake -> Processing -> Release -> Intake`.

The `Release -> Intake` transition completes exactly one batch and increments `completed_batches`. Calling `advance` while offline returns `Offline` without changing state. `stop` changes any active phase to `Offline`, preserves the completed count, and returns `Offline` without changing state if already offline. Starting after a stop always resumes at `Intake`.

`view` must return a detached value snapshot. Because `MachineView` is owned and copyable, a previously returned view must remain unchanged after later transitions and cannot provide an alias through which the machine can be mutated.

