Keep this exact public API:

```rust
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum DecodeEvent {
    Packet(Vec<u8>),
    Rejected,
}

pub struct PacketDecoder { /* private fields */ }

impl PacketDecoder {
    pub fn new() -> Self;
    pub fn push(&mut self, chunk: &[u8]) -> Vec<DecodeEvent>;
}
```

The decoder receives arbitrary chunks of a byte stream and retains incomplete data between calls. Each frame has:

- one byte `N`, the payload length;
- exactly `N` payload bytes;
- one checksum byte equal to the wrapping sum of the payload bytes.

`push` appends the chunk, processes every complete frame currently buffered, and returns events in stream order. A valid frame produces `DecodeEvent::Packet` with an owned payload. A complete frame with a wrong checksum produces `DecodeEvent::Rejected`. In either case, only that frame is consumed, so a malformed frame must not discard a valid frame following it in the same chunk. An incomplete trailing frame produces no event and remains buffered. Zero-length payloads are valid and have checksum zero.

Use only the Rust standard library. The implementation must be deterministic and perform no filesystem, network, clock, or random operations. Do not include a `main` function.

The current implementation loses buffered frames after malformed input:

```rust
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum DecodeEvent {
    Packet(Vec<u8>),
    Rejected,
}

pub struct PacketDecoder {
    buffer: Vec<u8>,
}

impl PacketDecoder {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self { buffer: Vec::new() }
    }

    pub fn push(&mut self, chunk: &[u8]) -> Vec<DecodeEvent> {
        self.buffer.extend_from_slice(chunk);
        let mut events = Vec::new();

        loop {
            let Some(&length_byte) = self.buffer.first() else {
                break;
            };
            let payload_len = length_byte as usize;
            let frame_len = payload_len + 2;
            if self.buffer.len() < frame_len {
                break;
            }

            let checksum = self.buffer[1..1 + payload_len]
                .iter()
                .fold(0u8, |sum, byte| sum.wrapping_add(*byte));
            let encoded_checksum = self.buffer[frame_len - 1];

            if checksum == encoded_checksum {
                events.push(DecodeEvent::Packet(
                    self.buffer[1..1 + payload_len].to_vec(),
                ));
                self.buffer.drain(..frame_len);
            } else {
                events.push(DecodeEvent::Rejected);
                self.buffer.clear();
                break;
            }
        }

        events
    }
}
