`push` appends the chunk, processes every complete frame currently buffered, and returns events in stream order. A valid frame produces `DecodeEvent::Packet` with an owned payload. A complete frame with a wrong checksum produces `DecodeEvent::Rejected`. In either case, only that frame is consumed, so a malformed frame must not discard a valid frame following it in the same chunk. An incomplete trailing frame produces no event and remains buffered. Zero-length payloads are valid and have checksum zero.

