{"items":[{"id":"cap-v2-stateful_workflows-rust-repair-02","problem":"A workflow accepts a script containing one command per line:

- `start NAME` transitions `Idle` to `Active { name: NAME, advances: 0 }`.
- `advance` increments `advances` while active.
- `finish` transitions an active workflow to `Completed` while retaining its name and advance count.

A command with the wrong number of tokens is malformed. A well-formed command that is not valid in the current phase is an invalid transition. Command indices are zero-based. Applying a script must be atomic: if any line is malformed or has an invalid transition, the workflow must return the appropriate error and retain exactly the phase it had before the call.

The following implementation violates that rollback requirement because commands preceding an erroneous line remain applied. Repair it and return a complete `solution.rs` exposing the same public API. Use only the Rust standard library. Do not add a `main` function or perform filesystem, network, clock, or random operations.

```rust
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum Phase {
    Idle,
    Active { name: String, advances: u64 },
    Completed { name: String, advances: u64 },
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum ApplyError {
    Malformed { command_index: usize },
    InvalidTransition { command_index: usize },
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Workflow {
    phase: Phase,
}

impl Workflow {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self { phase: Phase::Idle }
    }

    pub fn phase(&self) -> &Phase {
        &self.phase
    }

    pub fn apply_script(&mut self, script: &str) -> Result<(), ApplyError> {
        for (command_index, line) in script.lines().enumerate() {
            apply_line(&mut self.phase, line, command_index)?;
        }
        Ok(())
    }
}

fn apply_line(phase: &mut Phase, line: &str, command_index: usize) -> Result<(), ApplyError> {
    let fields: Vec<&str> = line.split_whitespace().collect();
    match fields.as_slice() {
        ["start", name] => match phase {
            Phase::Idle => {
                *phase = Phase::Active {
                    name: (*name).to_owned(),
                    advances: 0,
                };
                Ok(())
            }
            _ => Err(ApplyError::InvalidTransition { command_index }),
        },
        ["advance"] => match phase {
            Phase::Active { advances, .. } => {
                *advances += 1;
                Ok(())
            }
            _ => Err(ApplyError::InvalidTransition { command_index }),
        },
        ["finish"] => match phase {
            Phase::Active { name, advances } => {
                *phase = Phase::Completed {
                    name: name.clone(),
                    advances: *advances,
                };
                Ok(())
            }
            _ => Err(ApplyError::InvalidTransition { command_index }),
        },
        ["start", ..] | ["advance", ..] | ["finish", ..] | [] => {
            Err(ApplyError::Malformed { command_index })
        }
        _ => Err(ApplyError::Malformed { command_index }),
    }
}
