A command with the wrong number of tokens is malformed. A well-formed command that is not valid in the current phase is an invalid transition. Command indices are zero-based. Applying a script must be atomic: if any line is malformed or has an invalid transition, the workflow must return the appropriate error and retain exactly the phase it had before the call.

